== order sanity: n prime (MR-40), p prime, Hasse |p+1-n| <= 2 sqrt(p) (cofactor 1) ==
secp192k1        n_bits=192 n_prime=True p_prime=True hasse=True
secp224k1        n_bits=225 n_prime=True p_prime=True hasse=True
secp256k1        n_bits=256 n_prime=True p_prime=True hasse=True
P-256            n_bits=256 n_prime=True p_prime=True hasse=True
brainpoolP256r1  n_bits=256 n_prime=True p_prime=True hasse=True
P-384            n_bits=384 n_prime=True p_prime=True hasse=True
brainpoolP384r1  n_bits=384 n_prime=True p_prime=True hasse=True
P-521            n_bits=521 n_prime=True p_prime=True hasse=True

== exact n^4 vs f64::MAX = (2^53-1)*2^971 ==
curve            n_bits  n^4>MAX  log2(n^4/MAX)        n^4 - MAX sign / margin
secp192k1           192  False    -2.560000e+02
secp224k1           225  False    -1.280000e+02
secp256k1           256  True     +0.000000e+00
P-256               256  False    -1.343665e-09
brainpoolP256r1     256  False    -2.363054e+00
P-384               384  True     +5.120000e+02
brainpoolP384r1     384  True     +5.085469e+02
P-521               521  True     +1.060000e+03

threshold N* = min n with n^4 > f64::MAX: 2^256 - N* = 3213876088517980684888395375866072719838990621118340425318400 (~2^201.00)
  secp256k1        2^256 - n = ~2^128.35  -> above threshold
  P-256            2^256 - n = ~2^224.00  -> below threshold
  brainpoolP256r1  2^256 - n = ~2^254.43  -> below threshold
  float(secp256k1) == 2^256: True;  (float(n)^2)^2 = inf
  float(P-256) == 2^256: False;  (float(n)^2)^2 = 1.7976931331880837e+308
  float(brainpoolP256r1) == 2^256: False;  (float(n)^2)^2 = 3.4943426549439724e+307

